      "text": "{\"cli_catalog_available\":true,\"command\":null,\"content\":\"The 1.7.0 Workbench adds a secondary-sidebar transcript for direct local indexed queries, editable plans, evidence recipes, native schema-generated forms, cited source/context actions, copy/export and bounded local sessions. Use AIRK: Open Workbench in a trusted registered workspace. It does not run an agent or edit sources.\\nThe public parse tool uses schema airk.parse.request/1 and mode prepare (default) or execute. Supply exactly one of text, recipe or plan, and project when this connection has multiple configured projects. Explicit steps contain id, public tool, args and optional named bindings from earlier steps. capabilities.workbench publishes supported operation schemas and selectors. Native CLI uses airk parse TEXT, --execute, --project and --request FILE (or - for bounded stdin).\\nPlans retain exact collection/publication, scope, digest and budgets. At most six steps, twelve reads, twelve fan-out targets and 512 KiB; deadlines are checked between admitted synchronous reads. Uncertainty returns requires_input; partial results preserve failed/skipped steps, upstream clipping and continuation reasons. Stale prepared plans never silently switch to current evidence. No recursive plans, management, commands or source writes.\\nThe fixed intent model is trained offline on original phrasing, public repository vocabulary and attributed public query data. In this review build, supported learned requests produce inert proposed plans. Review the tool and inputs, then explicitly submit the plan to execute it. Rejection and ask-rate qualification remain incomplete; learned requests never execute automatically. References are textual occurrences and relationships are candidates, never proof of resolved callers or complete impact. Sessions contain local excerpts; persistence controls, clear and exports belong to the user. Reconnect existing agents after installing the matching 1.7.0 runtime. R